son":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102360","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102360","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102360.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102360.patch","merged_at":"2025-05-22T17:22:11Z"},"body":"I've implemented the `set_stream_position` operation for Theora video files and as a consequence also `get_length`. It also tries to comply with the documentation by not changing the current frame when `stop` is called and playing seamless loops.\r\n\r\nI've made a [simple videoplayer project](/berarma/godot-videoplayer) to help test video playing on Godot.\r\n\r\n- *Production edit: This closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/10148.\r\nSee also https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/14430\r\nand https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/57744.*\r\n\r\nUPDATE: I've done more testing and added a few more improvements/fixes:\r\n\r\n- Fix crackling sound when playing videos with 6 channels.\r\n- Add 8-channel audio support. (See https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/37536#issuecomment-2053667996)\r\n- Add stereo down-mixing when playing files with 4/6/8 channels.  (See https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/37536#issuecomment-2053667996)\r\n- Use a permanent audio buffer to avoid copying the same buffer again and again when the output buffer is full.\r\n- Dynamic audio buffer size adapted to the number of channels, up to 8K samples,.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","sta